<section class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">PRIVACY & SAFETY</span><h1>Your information matters.</h1><p>These notes describe the prototype, not a complete legal privacy policy.</p></section>
<div class="content-card"><h2>Prototype data handling</h2><p>Appointment requests and contact messages are stored in the local MySQL database. Symptom submissions store the selected symptom category, duration, severity, guidance level, and timestamp. Chatbot logs store only a response category; the submitted question text is not saved. Anyone with database access may be able to view stored records. Use fictional test information during development.</p><h2>Protect yourself</h2><ul class="nice-list"><li>Do not submit national ID numbers, passwords, full medical records, or other unnecessary sensitive information.</li><li>Use a unique database account with limited permissions for production; do not use the XAMPP root account.</li><li>Use HTTPS, access controls, retention limits, backups, and a security review before deployment.</li><li>Obtain informed consent and review applicable Rwanda privacy and health-data laws before collecting real patient data.</li></ul><h2>Medical safety</h2><p>The site cannot diagnose illness or prescribe medication. In an emergency, contact local emergency services or go to the nearest health facility immediately.</p></div>
